Implement one opt-in host-owned Docker contained-command executor as an AgentAdapter, not enabled in registry/CLI defaults or Graph recovery yet. This is a first controlled executor stop-proof slice; G25 remains in_progress. Do not conflate with full G15 recovery or real Linux all-package compatibility. Exact local Unix socket + pinned daemon ID; command fixed in constructor and image pinned by sha256 ID. Non-root private PID/network/IPC namespaces; no mounts/volumes/socket, read-only root, bounded /tmp tmpfs, drop ALL caps, no-new-privileges, no restart, no auto-remove. API via Node http unix socket, bounded request/output/timeout, no shell CLI. Journal root host-owned and inaccessible to container. Invocation ID is hashed for filesystem key; exclusive mkdir permanently consumes invocation, never retried after unknown; durable immutable launch record AFTER create before start stores full container ID, daemon ID, config digest and nonce bound to fixed command/image. Missing/incomplete launch record cannot prove absent/stopped. New host reads journal and matching container inspect, rejects wrong daemon/config/namespaces/labels/mounts/restart before mutation. Stop uses DELETE exact full container ID with force=true; only successful response plus verified same daemon ID and absence, then durable receipt permits stopped true. No missing-container optimistic proof: crash after removal before durable ACK leaves unknown. Removal is necessary to fence paused old host's late start; old start on removed full ID cannot resurrect it. Concurrent stop failure remains unknown unless another durable receipt exists. Stop receipt never proves business success. Normal execution polls inspect, gets exit status/bounded logs then removes and returns done status. Abort invokes authorized removal; adapter confirmStopped is fresh read-only check of exact receipt + daemon + absence. Separate sync authorize(start|stop|read) callbacks rechecked after async boundaries immediately before each mutation; input config snapshotted. Existing adapters unchanged, no API-level restart/resume/automatic cleanup. Journal receipt may be written after main run cancelled but retains truthful scoped evidence. Durable state not privileged evidence supplied by worker. Real tests in dedicated Colima osstack-graph-test profile: real shell/setsid descendants, supervisor SIGKILL then fresh process stop and verify, late old start must fail404, missing row/container/wrong config/daemon/revocation fail closed. No host filesystem writes by command: caller-provided pinned image must contain any code to test. Image creation/candidate staging and production Graph broker/G15 wiring are next slice. Need review of design with critical correctness blockers and minimal adjustments, especially cross-host late start and Docker deletion proof.

// AgentAdapter — every sub-agent (Claude Code, Codex CLI, DeepSeek, ...) implements
// this. The daemon's orchestrator picks one via policy.score() and feeds it tasks.
//
// Design decisions locked in plan v0.6:
//   E1: capability schema = Zod (single source of truth)
//   D11: invocation = streaming AsyncIterable<HermesEvent>
//        (events flow back to Hermes via the adapter, not buffered)
//   D5: cancellation is requested through invoke(task, signal). Stop evidence
//        is separate: aborting or rejecting the iterator does not prove exit.

import type { Capability, CostTier } from "@osstack/core";
import type { HermesEvent } from "@osstack/hermes-adapter";

/** Globally unique adapter identifier (e.g. "claude-code", "codex-cli"). */
export type AgentId = string;

export interface AgentAvailability {
  available: boolean;
  /** Stable preflight classification for control-plane decisions. */
  status?: "available" | "not_authenticated" | "installed_but_broken" | "not_installed";
  /** Human-readable reason when unavailable (missing key, bin not on PATH, ...). */
  reason?: string;
  /** Last successful probe time (unix seconds). */
  last_checked_at: number;
}

export interface AgentTask {
  /** Globally unique run id (allocated by the orchestrator, not the adapter). */
  run_id: string;
  /** Owning task this run belongs to. */
  task_id: string;
  /** Hermes session that originated the request (for event envelope). */
  session_id: string;
  /** Capability the orchestrator selected for this run. */
  capability_id: string;
  /** Free-form user prompt + any structured context the adapter understands. */
  prompt: string;
  context?: Record<string, unknown>;
}

export interface AgentRuntimeIdentity {
  adapter_id: string;
  adapter_version: string;
  auth_mode: string;
  provider_id: string;
  model_id: string;
  model_context_window?: number;
  reasoning_effort?: string;
  agent_profile?: string;
  binary_path_sha256?: string;
  evidence_source: "reported" | "configured" | "inferred";
}

export type AgentStopConfirmation =
  | { stopped: true; evidence: string }
  | { stopped: false };

export interface AgentAdapter {
  readonly id: AgentId;
  readonly display_name: string;
  readonly cost_tier: CostTier;

  /** Capabilities this adapter advertises. Read by policy.score(). */
  capabilities(): readonly Capability[];

  /**
   * Cheap reachability probe. Should NOT call the underlying LLM; just check
   * that we have credentials + the CLI/SDK is present. < 2s expected.
   */
  isAvailable(): Promise<AgentAvailability>;

  /** Runtime/provider evidence used by review and proof artifacts. */
  runtimeIdentity?(): Promise<AgentRuntimeIdentity>;

  /**
   * Execute the task and stream Hermes-shaped events until terminal. The
   * adapter is responsible for emitting `run.started` first and one of
   * `done` / `error` last; the daemon will refuse non-conforming streams.
   *
   * Implementations MUST honor an AbortSignal: when fired, stop the
   * underlying work, emit a final `done` with status "cancelled", and
   * close the iterator. Legacy adapters may emit that status on request alone;
   * it is NOT stop confirmation. Callers must tolerate uncooperative streams.
   */
  invoke(task: AgentTask, signal: AbortSignal): AsyncIterable<HermesEvent>;

  /**
   * Optional lifecycle evidence after cancellation of this exact invocation.
   * Return stopped:true only after observing that ALL owned work (including
   * subprocess descendants and remote side effects) has stopped. evidence is
   * a nonempty resource/receipt reference or description of that observation.
   * Signal delivery, iterator closure, and done(cancelled) alone are not proof.
   * May wait for an observation; callers bound the wait and treat absence,
   * rejection, or an unconfirmed result as requiring reconciliation.
   */
  confirmStopped?(runId: string): Promise<AgentStopConfirmation>;
}

// Resumable conversation support is deliberately a separate structural
// capability. See session.ts and isSessionCapableAdapter(): existing one-shot
// adapters continue to satisfy AgentAdapter without implementing fake resume.

/**
 * Helper base class: keeps the common fields and forces subclasses to
 * implement the streaming method. Adapters don't HAVE to subclass this —
 * the interface above is sufficient — but most will because boilerplate.
 */
export abstract class BaseAgentAdapter implements AgentAdapter {
  abstract readonly id: AgentId;
  abstract readonly display_name: string;
  abstract readonly cost_tier: CostTier;

  abstract capabilities(): readonly Capability[];
  abstract isAvailable(): Promise<AgentAvailability>;
  abstract invoke(task: AgentTask, signal: AbortSignal): AsyncIterable<HermesEvent>;
}
